\section{File format}{

\code{\link[=pro_request]{pro_request()}} writes one JSON file per API page.  For paginated queries
each file has the structure \verb{\{"results": [...], "meta": \{...\}\}}.  For
group-by queries the array field is \code{"group_by"}.  For single-record lookups
the file is a bare JSON object.  All three formats are handled automatically.
}

\section{Output layout}{

The subdirectory structure of \code{input_json} is preserved, with hive-partition
naming (\verb{query=<name>/}, \verb{query_l2=<name>/}, ...) so that Arrow/DuckDB can
read the result as a partitioned dataset.  A \code{page} column is added to each
record with a value derived from the source filename (or subdirectory for
multi-query inputs).

With \code{compact_parquet}, the page files of each query are combined into
files of up to that many records after the conversion (see
\code{\link[=pro_compact_parquet]{pro_compact_parquet()}}).
}

